// proofs/crypto/rng/rng_init.saw
//
// SAW driver for rng_init algorithmic verification (Tier A per
// ADR-0009).
//
// rng_init is HMAC_DRBG_Instantiate per NIST SP 800-90A Rev. 1
// §10.1.2.3. We discharge:
//   * `instantiate` is deterministic — same seed_material always
//     produces the same (K, V) post-instantiate state.
//   * The full NIST CAVP DRBGVS COUNT=0 KAT, which exercises
//     instantiate followed by generate-and-discard / generate-and-keep
//     (the `nist_count0_kat` property in HMACDRBG.cry implicitly
//     witnesses instantiate's correctness — if instantiate were wrong,
//     the post-instantiate K, V would diverge from NIST's reference
//     implementation and the second generate's output would not match
//     the published ReturnedBits). The KAT itself is proven in
//     rng_bytes.saw to keep the per-function SAW driver scoped.

import "HMACDRBG.cry";

print "[rng_init.saw] proving instantiate is deterministic (48-byte seed) ...";
prove_print z3 {{ \seed -> instantiate_deterministic seed }};
print "[rng_init.saw] instantiate: deterministic.";

print "[rng_init.saw] PASS";
